cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Markout in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Markout: does a short-horizon trading edge survive costs, fills and competition?"
abstract: >-
  Research code and tools for testing whether a short-horizon trading edge survives
  the spread, realistic queue-position fills, competing traders and the bias of
  trying many strategies: a LOBSTER and NASDAQ ITCH fill simulator in Python and
  C++17, honest-evaluation statistics (Deflated Sharpe ratio, PBO, stationary
  bootstrap, a run-once holdout guard) and the studies built on them.
authors:
